#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kbounce; is a single player arcade game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is played on a field, surrounded by wall, with two or more balls that "
"move about in the field bouncing off of wals. The player can build new "
"walls, decreasing the size of active field"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The goal of the game is to fill at least 75&percnt; of the field and advance "
"to the next level."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "How To Play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The player is presented a rectangular tiled field surrounded by wall. Two or "
"more balls move about in the field and bounce off of the walls. The object "
"of the game is to limit the size of room in which the balls are."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The size of the active area of the field is decreased by making new walls "
"that enclose areas without balls in them. To complete a level, the player "
"must decrease the size of the active field by at least 75&percnt; within the "
"time allowed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"New walls are built by clicking the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> mouse "
"button in an active area of the field, at which point two walls will begin "
"to grow in opposite directions from the square the mouse was clicked in. "
"Only one wall in each direction may be growing on the screen at any given "
"time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the mouse is on the field, the cursor is shown as a pair of arrows "
"pointing in opposite directions, either horizontally or vertically. The "
"arrows point in the direction the walls will grow when the "
"<mousebutton>left</mousebutton> is clicked. This direction can be changed by "
"clicking the <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A new wall has a <quote>head</quote> which moves away from the point where "
"the mouse was clicked. A wall is not permanent until this <quote>head</"
"quote> runs into another wall. If a ball collides with any part of the wall "
"except the head, before the head has run into another wall, the new wall "
"will disappear completely and one life will be lost. If a ball collides with "
"the head in the direction of the wall's growth, the wall will stop growing "
"there, and become permanent, with no loss of life. If a ball collides with "
"the head from any other side, the ball will bounce off and the wall will "
"continue to grow normally."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Rules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The game starts with level 1 in which two balls move about in the field. The "
"player has two lifes and 90 seconds to successfully complete the level."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In n-th level there are n + 1 balls. The player is given n + 1 lives. They "
"have 30 * ( n + 2 ) seconds to complete it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a ball collides with a growing wall the player looses one life. An "
"exception is the collision with wall's <quote>head</quote> when no life is "
"lost."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The goal of each level is to cover at least 75&percnt; of the field with "
"wall."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The loss of all lives and exceeding the time alloted result in the end of "
"the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a player completes a level he receives 15 points for each life left, and "
"bonus depending on the number of balls and the number of tiles filled above "
"75&percnt;. They also advance to the next level."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Strategies and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many players find the game becomes quite difficult by only the third or "
"fourth level, given the number of balls on the field at once."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The trick to playing &kbounce; successfully is to build <quote>corridors</"
"quote>. To build a corridor, start a pair of walls growing close to another "
"wall, and time it such that one of the walls will be hit by a ball and one "
"of the walls will not, and thus become permanent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Building a corridor</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Building a corridor</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will leave a narrow corridor only a few squares high on the field, "
"surrounded on three sides by walls. Wait for the balls to bounce into the "
"open end of the corridor, and close the corridor behind the ball with a new "
"wall. Although you will most likely lose a life for each corridor created, "
"you can trap several balls in a single corridor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Capturing balls in a corridor</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Capturing balls in a corridor</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A final tip &mdash; take your time! There is plenty of time, as shown in the "
"<guilabel>Time</guilabel> display at the bottom of the screen. Rushing will "
"just get you in trouble!"
msgstr ""

